<title>FRANCE: Tietmeyer says welcomes Italy EMU entry.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer says welcomes Italy EMU entry.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said on Wednesday that he would welcome Italy's participation as a founder of European Economic and Monetary Union as long as it met Maastricht treaty criteria in a lasting way.</p>
<p>&quot;Italy is undertaking considerable efforts to resolve its problems and that is positive,&quot; he told daily Le Monde in an interview.</p>
<p>&quot;If Italy fulfills the criteria in a lasting way it will of course be welcome in the community of the euro. We must not point the finger at this or that country, but rather we take note with pleasure that all countries are making great efforts to fulfill the required conditions.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
